You don't need scrolls or mirrors.  You are not fighting medusa.  The
cockatrice has you paranoid.  This is not so hard!

Spoiler ahead:


You need a pair of gloves.  These seem easy enough to find by killing
soldiers or other critters with lots of armor.

It is also nice to have a lizard corpse or two, just in case.

If you don't have gloves, then a big supply of missile weapons (knives,
darts, arrows, etc.) will work.

All you need to do is make sure you never touch it bare-handed.  Sometimes
you may start "feeling stiff" while you are fighting a cockatrice.  If so,
that is the time to eat your lizard corpse.  You may have noticed that lizard
corpses don't decay like most others.  They are the remedy for stiff limbs.
Fail to eat one when required, and you will soon become a monument to
yourself.   ;^)

If you have gloves, just wield your favorite weapon and whack away at it.
Once you've killed it, it is fun to pick it up and wield it.  I usually
try to descend a couple of levels deeper immediately after I kill a
cockatrice.  One blow from it and your enemy becomes a statue.  This can
help you gain experience levels faster.  Be prepared to run away to safety,
though.  After a while your cockatrice corpse will rot, and then you may
need to retreat to safer environs.

PS - if you are wielding a cockatrice, be sure you don't carry enough baggage
     to make you "fall down the stairs".  You can get stoned by falling down,
     even while wearing gloves.

